<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila teissieri Turing wavelength at 1.7 µm (detail scale s0, Holocene 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Each modelling step is a function whose docstring names the Turing or Schnakenberg relation. Pass 2 adds sigma_peak_wavelength and rendered_frame_ks beside the original dispersion and renderer. Lean theorems pin the trace sign, the drive sign, the 12-wavelength domain, and the predecessor and successor inequalities." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila teissieri Turing wavelength at 1.7 µm (detail scale s0, Holocene 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg kinetics and the Turing wavenumber formula are implemented directly, with D_u solved so λ_c = 1.72 µm. Trace < 0, det > 0, σ(0) < 0, σ(k_c) > 0. Linearised growth matches continuum σ(k) at Pearson r = 0.9935. Pass 2 separates that formula wavelength from argmax σ(k) = 1.985 µm instead of forcing them to agree." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila teissieri Turing wavelength at 1.7 µm (detail scale s0, Holocene 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion RMSE is 0.030 1/s. The saturated wavelength (1.903 µm) is 4.2% from the growth-rate peak and is not substituted for the 1.72 µm formula value. Specimen Otsu area, circularity, aspect and coherency differ from the activator mask. Rendered-frame KS and activator-vs-micrograph KS are both reported against a 0.05 reference they do not equal. An 18-wavelength domain selects a higher mode (17) than the 12-wavelength patch (11)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
