    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila teissieri specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila teissieri" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That D. virilis descends from D. teissieri.",
        "does_not_claim: That a second assessor or a Commons photograph was obtained.",
        "does_not_claim: That the nonlinear pattern must sit on the formula wavelength. It tracks the growth-rate peak (1.985 µm) more closely than the determinant shortcut (1.72 µm).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: (a, b, gamma, Dv/Du) = (0.13, 0.91, 1.15, 17.4) so the formula wavelength is 1.72 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: σ(k) peak, rendered-frame KS, equal-diffusion and autocatalysis ablations, diffusivity sweep.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 reaction terms a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Tsacas 1971 name Drosophila teissieri, confirmed at GBIF 5074619.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and the unequal-diffusivity condition.",
        "transfer_boundary: 1.72 µm is the campaign detail-scale assignment, not a published teissieri measurement.",
        "transfer_boundary: Predecessor 97.6 µm and successor floor 2.72 µm are atlas contrasts at 0 Ma." ;
